  "question": {
    "text": "A solid sphere, of radius R acquires a terminal velocity <math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> when falling (due to gravity) through a viscous fluid having a coefficient of viscosity <math><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The sphere is broken into 27 identical solid spheres. If each of these spheres acquires a terminal velocity, <math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></math> when falling through the same fluid, the ratio <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> equals:",
